Author: Erica Moszkowski <erica.moszkowski@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 15:42:32 2015 -0400

    Create separate test for eigenvalue decomposition to deal with nonsingular hessians
    
    This mostly solves issue #1 in Eig.jl - namely, that `Pkg.test("DSGE")` and
    `include("runtests.jl")` produced different results for
    metropolis_hastings.jl.
    
    To paraphrase @andreasnoack:
    
    Eigenvectors of decomposition of singular matrices are not well
    determined (because eigenvalues are effectively zero). Therefore,
    small pertubations can change eigenvectors a lot. The number of
    threads used by BLAS are set differently when you run `Pkg.test()`
    than when you run `include("runtests.jl")`, and this slightly changes
    the computation of the eigenvectors.
    
    Because this is such a specific problem that could potentially affect
    a lot of our end users, we add a new test for eigenvalue decomposition
    to the test suite. In that test, we force the machine to only use 1
    thread by calling `addprocs` before doing the eigenvalue decomposition.
    
    The metropolis_hastings test has been refigured to read in the
    covariance matrix of the proposal distribution directly. Therefore, if
    there are problems with `eig.jl` and not with
    `metropolis_hastings.jl`, we'll know that we haven't introduced any
    bugs into metropolis_hastings.
    
    TODO: Set appropriate thresholds for relative differences between expected and actual eig.jl output.

